<http://data.silknow.org/object/4f5909a5-63c5-3d7c-96bb-58606efc4322/observation/5>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/historical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "The eighteenth century home of the Burninghams was Hussey's farm. Henry's son, Thomas Burningham, became a wealthy landowner, and built Froyle House near Alton, Hamptonshire. The estate extended to nearly 1050 acres, including gardens, parkland, woodland, five farms, small holdings and cottages. Most of the household contents remained in the family until the mid-nineteenth century."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/4f5909a5-63c5-3d7c-96bb-58606efc4322> .

